  "details": "Not sure if this is the same for others, or on which end this is on, but it's worth sharing.\n\nI've noticed that, along with the loading screens and hitches, opening my menus seem to cause a loss of tracking on my trackers. This seemed to occasionally happen in live too, but much more rarely. Here it happens frequently. I open social or world menu? And bam, I'm flying off hip first into the ground or sky for a brief moment before snapping back. (The process usually repeats too, it's not one and done.)\n\nWorth noting however, is the following caveat; which is that I am using the oculus + vive trackers hybrid setup, so I'm not sure if the problem is the same for vive FBT users\n\nAlso, this is with just one lighthouse on, and in perfect view of it. So it's not a matter of lighthouses arguing or some such issue. There is normally absolutely no tracking loss outside of the menu, but when it opens, there it is.",
